--- a/docs/notes.md
+++ b/docs/notes.md
@@ -153,3 +153,86 @@ game yet (no join codes, no big-screen stage, no websockets/sse).
 "Question X of Y", "Answers: A / B", "Correct" (option mark), "The quiz is
 over", "Your name", "Join", "Hi, <name>!", "Your answer", "Correct!",
 "Wrong!", "No answer".
+
+## Prizes release (winners, scoring, leaderboard)
+
+### Model
+
+- `quizzes.winners INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 3` — the "Number of winners"
+  setting (validated ≥ 1 in the quiz form; `create_quiz`/`update_quiz` also
+  clamp with `max(1)`). The **export/import format is intentionally
+  unchanged** (exactly `title` + `questions`); imported quizzes get the
+  default of 3.
+- `answers.answered_ms INTEGER` — ms since the unix epoch of the player's
+  last pick (set on insert and on the ON CONFLICT re-pick update, from
+  Rust's `SystemTime` — one server clock for everything).
+- New table `question_opens (game_id, question_id, opened_ms)` — the moment
+  the moderator opened the question in that game (set in
+  `db::game_show_question`, which covers both "start" and "next").
+  FKs cascade with the game/question.
+- `players.winner INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` — the picked winners.
+- Migrations for databases from older releases: `ensure_column` does
+  `PRAGMA table_info` + `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` when missing (the new
+  table needs no ALTER thanks to CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS). Verified with
+  a hand-built legacy DB.
+
+### Scoring (`db::leaderboard`)
+
+- One row per player of the game: points = number of correct answers to
+  questions actually opened in this game (join through `question_opens`),
+  time = total ms of those correct answers (open → last pick; `MAX(...,0)`
+  guards clock skew).
+- Order: points DESC, time ASC (speed breaks ties), player id ASC (stable).
+- Points are never shown during the game: the playing fragments (phone and
+  big screen) contain no points — only verdicts/answer counts.
+
+### Winner picking (`game::pick_top` / `pick_draw`, on the finished game)
+
+- "Top N": first N of the leaderboard, but 0-point players never win.
+- "Draw": everyone with more points than the N-th place wins; the remaining
+  N−k prizes are drawn at random (Fisher-Yates on /dev/urandom) among the
+  players with exactly the N-th place's points. If the N-th place has 0
+  points (or there is no N-th place), nobody is drawn — 0-point players
+  never win, so "fewer than N players with points ⇒ all of them win".
+  Every click re-draws and replaces the winner set.
+- "Reset winners": clears the flags.
+- All three are `action=top|draw|reset` on the existing
+  `POST .../games/{gid}/action` endpoint, accepted only in `finished`.
+
+### Views
+
+- Quiz form ("New quiz" / "Settings"): new `type="number"` input
+  `name="winners"` with `<label for="quiz-winners">Number of winners</label>`,
+  min 1, step 1, default value 3. Invalid input re-renders with
+  "Number of winners must be at least 1" (and "Enter a title").
+- Big screen, finished: `<ol class="leaderboard">` of `<li class="leader">`
+  (place / name / "N points"), winners get `is-winner` + a pink
+  `<span class="leader__badge">Winner</span>` (note the leading space so
+  `innerText` reads "Ann Winner"). Controls: "Top N" (pink), "Draw",
+  "Reset winners" — no confirm() on any of them (QA clicks directly).
+- Phone, finished: `.result-card` with "Place X of Y" (one element,
+  contiguous text), the big place number, and "N points"
+  (`points_label`: "2 points" / "1 point" / "0 points"); winners also get
+  `<div class="winner-banner">You won!</div>`. A space was added before the
+  badge for readable innerText.
+- Liveness: the polling interval in `LIVE_JS` went from 1000 ms to 250 ms —
+  ties are decided by speed, so every screen must follow the moderator
+  close to instantly (measured ~0.2 s in headless Chromium).
+
+### QA-facing contract (new labels, keep stable)
+
+"Number of winners", "Leaderboard", "Top N" (e.g. "Top 3"), "Draw",
+"Reset winners", "Winner" (badge), "You won!", "Place X of Y",
+"2 points" / "1 point" / "0 points". Leaderboard rows are `li.leader`
+inside `ol.leaderboard`. Error: "Number of winners must be at least 1".
+
+### Testing
+
+- `cargo test`: winner-picking edge cases (ties, zeros, N > players, draw
+  varies) + leaderboard ordering/points/time on an in-memory DB.
+- `test/e2e.sh` (43 curl checks): settings field + validation, full game
+  with 4 players (incl. a 0-point one), leaderboard content/order, phone
+  places/points, Top 2 / Reset / Draw incl. re-draws, no points mid-game.
+- `test/browser_test.py` (+ `test/cdp.py`, a dependency-free CDP driver):
+  real Chromium — join flow, live latencies (~0.2 s), Top/Draw/Reset
+  updating stage and both phones live.
